WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.200
There's a

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.001
new controversy

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:01.935
tonight involving

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:04.004
Supreme Court Justice Clarence Thomas.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.538
ProPublica is now reporting

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.007
in an in-depth story

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.708
that for more than two decades,

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.176
Justice Thomas and his wife,

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.177
Ginni Thomas,

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.513
have secretly accepted luxury trips

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.615
from the billionaire Republican donor,

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.783
Harlan Crow.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.318
These trips include flights

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.753
on his private jet

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.788
cruising on his super yacht,

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.423
also going to far flung places

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.891
like a trip in Indonesia.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.059
Sales in 19,

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:26.926
as well as trips

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.661
to an exclusive All-Male retreat

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.429
in California.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.498
That's known as the Bohemian Grove.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:32.265
Josh Caplan

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.266
is one of the ProPublica

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.101
reporters who broke this story.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.735
And luckily,

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.405
he joins us now at this table.

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.440
This story is kind of rocked

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.575
the not just New York of

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.777
Washington, Phil, as well.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.512
I think you would agree.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.880
Tell us what your reporting found.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.214
Yes.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:48.782
So we

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.151
found that Clarence Thomas has

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.353
been taking luxury trips

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.255
from a billionaire real estate

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.991
magnate and Republican Megadonor

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.629
virtually every year for over 20 years.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.865
And as as you said, private jet

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:06.933
flights around the world,

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.134
international yacht

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.335
cruises

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.172
regular trips to a private resort,

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:13.940
invitation only, you know,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.209
staffed by private chefs.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:16.943
The Indonesia trip,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:17.844
you mentioned

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.212
he this is in 2019

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.880
just one recent example

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.083
he flew Thomas flew on the billionaire's

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.150
private jet

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.285
to Indonesia

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:25.685
and spent

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:26.619
nine days island

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.555
hopping on a super yacht

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.957
staff by you know with a full staff

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.592
the day after the court finished its term

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.326
that couple of days

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.060
a couple of days

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.795
and yeah if we were told that

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.764
if Thomas had chartered that itself

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.800
it would have cost at least $500,000,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.803
$500,000.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.505
It's a it's a nice private jet.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.906
But that's not how you travel.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.642
That is not how I roll at all.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.711
So this ethics related to Supreme

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.445
Court has been kind

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.947
of a bubbling issue in Congress

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.415
for a number of years now.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.015
There are some bills

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:56.916
that have already been proposed.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:57.851
I think your story is probably

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.419
going to lose a few more,

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.420
to say the least.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.455
But can you explain to people why

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:04.557
even the parts that

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.092
I think right now are up in the air

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:06.726
as to whether or not

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.361
they were legal or problematic?

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.229
Why Supreme Court

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.663
justices could do something like this,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.898
not have to report it

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.233
and have nobody know were it

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.635
not for your investigation?

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.136
Yes.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:16.569
So, I mean,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.872
I think one of the root issues here

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.206
is that

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.041
Supreme Court justices face

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.810
very little transparency

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.045
and very little oversight compared to

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.282
essentially every other member

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.117
of the federal government

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.520
where, you know, I mean, for instance,

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.623
while it is experts told us that appears

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.157
to violated

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:37.991
the law, that he didn't

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.926
disclose these trips,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.361
there are no restrictions, really,

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:42.295
or there are few restrictions

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.897
on what gifts justices can accept.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.798
And that's a really stark contrast

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.000
from the other branches of government.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.003
So, you know,

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:50.570
essentially, I

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.172
mean, the Supreme Court has for a while

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:52.605
been left

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.674
to almost entirely to police itself.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.643
You know what I find interesting?

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.545
Lower courts can be policed,

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.379
if you will, by Congress,

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.114
because Congress can post

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.016
ethics rules on lower courts.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.484
The Supreme Court

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.251
is deemed

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.353
and put in place by the Constitution

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.590
and nobody has a rules of ethics

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.458
at the Supreme.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.326
Let me say that again.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.061
The Supreme Court,

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.829
the highest court in the land.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:17.730
It literally

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.932
it blows my mind

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.333
to think about that, that

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.568
there are no rules

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:23.102
that they have decided among themselves.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:23.736
They could say, listen,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.772
we have got to have something in place.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.173
If for nothing else,

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.075
then the word legitimacy,

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.577
because everyone is worried

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.679
about all of the different problems

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.013
with sort of the government

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:34.714
and whether or not

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:35.949
they're going to see this quarter

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:38.851
any further court as a legitimate court.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.086
If they can't police themselves,

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.221
why are they police or not?

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.355
Well, this this goes to,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.490
you know, the founders and the framers.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.291
They recognize

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.559
that you have to have what they call

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.760
Republican virtues,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.761
not capital or Republican,

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.796
but virtues

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:52.665
that support having a republic, having

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.201
the rule of law, having democracy.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.669
And they didn't think

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:57.303
that you would actually

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.571
have to tell people

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.907
not to take $500,000 of like,

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.442
you know, fund trips and not report on it

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.176
because there was

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.644
this idea that you would have virtues

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.680
along side of the words

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.581
that are written down.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.415
And one of the things I think

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.316
is really interesting

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:10.950
is that when you hear

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.518
from Clarence Thomas,

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.121
when he speaks, he speaks so much about

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:18.358
virtues, ethics, morality, etc.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.460
It's his main grievance

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.094
against the country

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.195
that people are getting away

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:23.162
from those values.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.497
And yet in his own life,

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.499
he's not practicing the values

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:29.002
of transparency, of ethical conduct.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.170
And so it causes a real,

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.405
I think, problem for the country

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.340
when they are not policing themselves.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.775
And in fact, they are

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.943
yelling at the rest of us for doing stuff

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.211
they're not doing on their own.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:39.445
What's what's the defense

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.247
that you're hearing from

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.015
Clarence Thomas

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.783
or the Supreme Court on this?

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:44.851
So Clarence Thomas,

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.653
we sent him detailed questions,

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:48.521
follow up repeatedly.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.023
He didn't respond.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.758
So we haven't heard from Thomas,

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:54.260
but the his friend, the billionaire

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.695
Harlan Crow,

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.163
told us they're very dear friends.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:57.597
And, you know,

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:58.164
he acknowledged

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:00.400
that his extended hospitality

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.435
to Thomas over the years, but said, No.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.603
One, that Thomas hadn't

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.404
asked for any of it.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.272
And also that it was no different

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.540
than what he's extended

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.509
to his many other dear friends.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.443
Can I just quickly ask,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.512
was there any case that you found

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.279
where

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:17.183
perhaps there was a conflict of interest

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:18.985
that Clarence Thomas looked

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.620
at that involved

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.255
any business dealings with his

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:24.457
his friend, his very wealthy friend?

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:24.924
Yeah, I mean,

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:27.160
so Caro has never personally

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.729
had a case before the Supreme Court.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.432
Most people don't, or at least not

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.132
very often

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.336
he but I mean,

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.237
but he does have vast

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.340
financial and ideological interests.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.344
So he's one he is a enormously

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.979
successful business figure.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.982
And also he's

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.552
given millions of dollars

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.953
to ideological efforts

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.155
to shape the judiciary, to shape the law,

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.225
including the Federalist Society.

00:05:59.225 --> 00:05:59.659
You know, he's

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:02.095
also he sits on the board of major

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:05.264
think tanks that publish

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.166
conservative legal scholarship

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.435
that's advancing specific theories.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.470
Their scholars

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.304
occasionally file

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.606
amicus briefs to the Supreme Court.

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:14.741
So it's a complicated question.

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:15.041
And it's

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:16.175
I also should note that, you know,

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.844
he's given ten you know,

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.346
over $10 million in disclosed donations.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.214
But we know he's also

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.215
given to dark money groups.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.149
And so it's

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.450
you know, to a certain extent,

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.319
there's an unknown there, safe to say.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:26.886
I mean, Clarence

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.554
Thomas is no stranger to scrutiny.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:29.355
Neither is his wife.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:29.922
And safe to say

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.290
this is only adding to it.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.759
Josh Kaplan, thanks for your reporting

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:33.926
and thanks for sharing it with us today.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:34.894
Thanks so much for having me.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:35.862
The other remarkable story

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:36.929
we're talking about this morning

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.431
is this ProPublica report

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.699
into Supreme Court Justice

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:40.600
Clarence Thomas

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.001
and these luxury trips

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:42.402
that he and

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:42.869
his wife

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.670
took with a Republican megadonor,

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.406
which the donor says

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:47.807
that was just hospitality.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:49.709
It wasn't anything that Justice

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:50.576
Thomas had asked for.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:52.578
Justice Thomas himself has not commented

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.781
and there's no formal code of conduct

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.615
at the Supreme Court

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:57.417
that would bar him from doing this.

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:58.384
But I wonder if this makes

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:59.852
you think there needs to be

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.120
tighter restrictions

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.455
on the ethics code

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:04.457
for someone like a Supreme Court justice?

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:06.392
Well, first of all, I

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:08.327
don't know if the facts of the report,

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:09.462
the reporting is accurate.

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:11.063
I assume it is, but parts of

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:12.832
it may not be accurate.

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:14.801
And it and I know Justice Thomas,

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:16.068
I talked with a lot of people,

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:17.336
hard people that would know him

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.638
extremely well.

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:21.307
I don't think this kind of action

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.209
would in any way influence

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:24.377
his decision on the court.

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:26.279
But having said all that,

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:29.215
I worry about the image,

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.751
the fact that a justice's

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:34.020
is taking these gifts

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.188
and not reporting it

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:38.191
if, in fact, the law requires reporting.

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:40.359
And if the reason you don't report

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:41.928
is because you're afraid of how it looks,

00:07:41.928 --> 00:07:43.529
maybe you shouldn't accept it.

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.565
Again, I don't think it has any influence

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:46.599
or impact

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:47.834
on the work of the justice,

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:51.270
but I think it's creates further

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:53.372
angst about the court,

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.874
about the justices.

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.476
Obviously, given the recent decisions

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:57.944
at the end of the last term,

00:07:57.944 --> 00:07:59.579
a lot of people have raised questions

00:07:59.579 --> 00:08:01.781
about about the court

00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:02.982
talks about expanding,

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.350
the court talks about term

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.918
limits, talk about limiting

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:07.553
the jurisdiction of the court.

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.121
So I think the

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.356
justices need to be careful

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.491
because it's not all about

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:13.326
just your individual conduct.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:15.361
Whatever you do, whatever you say,

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:17.230
it affects the rest of the justices.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.632
It affects the reputation of the court.

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:22.535
And I think if you look at recent polling

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.003
and the judges generally should,

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.104
I would say, urge them

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:26.973
not to look at recent polling

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:28.307
because they need to make their decisions

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:29.208
based on what they believe

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.710
is right, believe

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.011
based upon what the Constitution

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.346
or the statutes say.

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:34.080
But nonetheless,

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:34.981
you need to be sensitive

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:37.216
about how your actions affect how people

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:40.520
believe or respect the court

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.588
because in the end, respect

